                <pb facs="0797" n="687" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg687"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/3219: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-12-16T16:00:00+08:00">December 16, 1931—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 16—10:45 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>1084. Following from American Consul General at Mukden: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“December 15, 11 p.m. Tsang Shih-yi, Chairman of this Province, who has
                            been under detention since September 18 at Mukden was released Sunday
                            and according to reliable information, he was installed as Governor late
                            this afternoon. In my opinion this event foreshadows an early attack on
                            Chinchow.</p>
                        <p>Confirmation to follow.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Repeated to Minister at Nanking and Military Attaché at Chinchow.</p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
